{"skill":{"slug":"byterover","displayName":"ByteRover"},"version":{"version":"3.3.0","createdAt":1776512227733,"changelog":"# v3.3.0\n\n## Added\n\n- Added section 11 \"Query and Curate History\" with Overview, Use/Do-NOT-use blocks, and both brv curate view and brv query-log view command references\n- Removed the curate history block from section 3.\n\n## Unchanged\n\n- All existing commands (query, search, curate, review, providers, locations, vc, swarm) remain unchanged from v3.2.0.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":20422,"sha256":"89a7e1ee8a10571c06a4fa3464fb4a4ab57ab9fb3c271298bba9c9313e66dba3","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2346,"sha256":"4d0430748daf7410ffb98ed1a9d594a10b9509dfec56594f374b9afaeaafa0cf","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789021991044,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"fc455bdaba88b0cc8417ad70891b51b5e625baebface141d7a3e9c122bab608f","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/fc455bdaba88b0cc8417ad70891b51b5e625baebface141d7a3e9c122bab608f","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: byterover\nVersion: 3.3.0\n\nThe 'byterover' skill bundle describes a comprehensive knowledge management system for AI agents, utilizing a CLI tool (`brv`) to manage project context via local Markdown files and Git-based version control. While the skill requires the installation of an external package (`byterover-cli`) and handles sensitive operations such as LLM API key configuration and remote data synchronization to `byterover.dev`, these capabilities are explicitly documented and directly support the stated purpose of the tool. No evidence of malicious intent, unauthorized data exfiltration, or harmful prompt injection was found in SKILL.md or _meta.json.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160121579},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":60,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":4,"checkedAt":1789021991044},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is for project memory, but it broadly directs agents to send project context to LLM providers and persist new memory, so it should be reviewed before installation.","dimensions":[{"detail":"brv query and brv curate are disclosed as sending query text, selected context, and included project files to a configured LLM provider; file reads are project-scoped and capped at 5 files, but automatic/broad use is not well contained.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The package contains only SKILL.md, but it instructs users to install byterover-cli globally with an unpinned npm command.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifact says the skill MUST be used before any work, tells agents to run brv query before thinking, and run brv curate after implementing, which is broader than user-directed memory management.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill intentionally writes long-term Markdown memory under .brv/context-tree and can curate to configured external memory providers; review controls exist for some pending changes, but routine post-task curation is not clearly user-approved per write.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The commands are coherent with a ByteRover project-knowledge skill: query, search, curate, review, version control, provider setup, and history all relate to managing project memory.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable with a memory tool that may send project context to a configured LLM provider and write persistent project memory. Prefer local search when possible, review what files or context are being sent, avoid secrets and sensitive source files, require approval before curation or cloud sync, and pin or independently verify the CLI package before global installation.","findings":"[EA5] expected: External provider setup is expected for LLM-backed memory queries, but the raw API-key command example and third-party provider use are sensitive and need user care.\n[P3] expected: Sending context to an LLM provider is disclosed and purpose-aligned, but broad pre-task query and file-backed curate instructions make this a material data-exposure concern.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: The unconditional 'before any work' activation is not necessary for a memory-management skill and materially expands when the tool may run.\n[T01] unexpected: The static finding is supported in part: mandatory workflow language can change unrelated agent workflows, though it does not show deception or malicious override behavior.\n[T05] expected: The artifact discloses project-scoped file access and LLM-provider processing; this is expected for the feature but still high-impact without per-operation consent and payload review.\n[T02] expected: Persistent memory is the skill's core purpose, but automatic curation after implementation can preserve incorrect or attacker-influenced context for future sessions.\n[T08] expected: A CLI install is expected, and no embedded malicious package is present in the artifact, but the unpinned global npm install is a supply-chain risk.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789021991044}}}}}